  "generated_text": "Let $t = \\frac{x}{x - 2}.$  Then $x = \\frac{2t}{t - 1}.$  Substituting this into the given equation, we get\n\\[\\left( \\frac{2t}{t - 1} \\right)^2 + 4 \\left( \\frac{2t}{t - 1} \\right)^2 = 45.\\]Simplifying, we get\n\\[\\frac{4t^2}{(t - 1)^2} + \\frac{16t^2}{(t - 1)^2} = 45.\\]Combining the fractions, we get\n\\[\\frac{20t^2}{(t - 1)^2} = 45.\\]Multiplying both sides by $(t - 1)^2,$ we get\n\\[20t^2 = 45(t - 1)^2.\\]Expanding and simplifying, we get\n\\[20t^2 = 45t^2 - 90t + 45.\\]Solving for $t,$ we get $t = \\boxed{3}.$",
